{"format":1,"key":"zone:thousandneedles","path":"/lore/zone/thousandneedles","name":"Thousand Needles","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"thousandneedles","name":"Thousand Needles","path":"/lore/zone/thousandneedles"},"levels":"Levels 25-35","description":"Thousand Needles is a sprawling canyon of sheer sandstone pillars and sunbaked salt pans in southern Kalimdor. Tauren tribes cling to settlements atop…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:thousandneedles","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Thousand Needles is a sprawling canyon of sheer sandstone pillars and sunbaked salt pans in southern Kalimdor. Tauren tribes cling to settlements atop towering mesas to escape aggressive centaur packs, while gnomish and goblin tinkerers run high-speed rocket cars across the dried-up seabed of the Shimmering Flats.","Before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, this territory was a lush river canyon fed by inland waterways flowing out toward the sea. The cataclysm tore the continent apart, thrusting the riverbed above the water table and altering the river's path until only dry stone and sandstone spires remained. Today, dozens of slender cylindrical columns rise from the canyon floor like a petrified forest. Tauren settled on the summits, stringing precarious rope bridges between peaks to establish villages out of reach of the hostile centaur marauders patrolling the shadow-draped canyon floor below.","Atop the needle-like spires, life is far from peaceful. At Freewind Post, tauren loyal to the Horde contend not only with predatory wind serpents and wyverns from Highperch, but also with their treacherous kin: the militant Grimtotem clan entrenched at Darkcloud Pinnacle. Cliffwatcher Longhorn oversees the defense of the plateau, seeking bold fighters to strike at Grimtotem agitators and secure the fragile bridges linking the peaks. To the north, the enormous mechanical winches of the Great Lift carry travelers down from the southern Barrens, though crossing the canyon floor remains a deadly gambit.","To the southeast, the canyon walls peel back into the Shimmering Flats, an enormous, desiccated salt pan sitting below sea level. In this harsh, blinding white expanse, gnomes and goblins maintain an uneasy neutrality around the Mirage Raceway. Rival engineers Pozzik and Fizzle Brassbolts race experimental rocket cars across the hard salt to settle which race possesses technological superiority. The pit stop attracts scoundrels, swindlers like Kravel Koalbeard, and hunters hunting the hardy scorpions, turtles, and basilisks that roam the searing basin."],"hash":"3fb560","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"fd6e946c9e","sec":122},"female-narrator":{"sha":"7f8717d443","sec":129}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Thousand Needles (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thousand_Needles_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Thousand Needles","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thousand_Needles"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/freewind-post","n":"Freewind Post","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/shimmering-flats","n":"Shimmering Flats","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/mirage-raceway","n":"Mirage Raceway","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/great-lift","n":"Great Lift","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkcloud-pinnacle","n":"Darkcloud Pinnacle","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/barrens","n":"The Barrens","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/feralas","n":"Feralas","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/tanaris","n":"Tanaris","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1802-tome-of-the-cabal","n":"Tome of the Cabal","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/item/tattered-manuscript","n":"Tattered Manuscript","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1803-tome-of-the-cabal","n":"Tome of the Cabal","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1135-highperch-venom","n":"Highperch Venom","k":"quest"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/camp-e-thok","n":"Camp E'thok","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkcloud-pinnacle","n":"Darkcloud Pinnacle","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subz